GET /podcast/episodesByIds IPodcastService.getEpisodesByIds | Read several episodes at once, in the order of the given identifiers, each with the listening position of the user. Unknown identifiers are skipped. At most 500 identifiers. | podcast | UserAuth | episodeIds:query | body:no
DELETE /podcast/import/{episodeId} IPodcastService.removeImport | Delete the stored audio of an episode of a feed show. The episode itself stays and is played from its origin afterwards. Episodes of the local podcast library cannot be removed this way, as that would delete the file of the user. | podcast | UserAuth | episodeId:path | body:no
POST /podcast/importEpisode/{episodeId} IPodcastService.importEpisode | Queue a single episode to be stored on the server. The transfer itself runs in the background, so the returned episode usually reports that its import is queued. | podcast | UserAuth | episodeId:path | body:no
GET /podcast/inProgress IPodcastService.getInProgress | Read the episodes the user started but did not finish, the most recently played one first. | podcast | UserAuth | page:query,pageSize:query | body:no
GET /podcast/lastPlayed IPodcastService.getLastPlayed | Read the episode the user played most recently, with the listening position, so a client can offer to continue it. Returns null if the user never played an episode. | podcast | UserAuth | includeCompleted:query | body:no
GET /podcast/latestEpisodes IPodcastService.getLatestEpisodes | Read the newest episodes across the shows the user is subscribed to, newest first. | podcast | UserAuth | page:query,pageSize:query | body:no
GET /podcast/observeProgress IPodcastService.observeProgress | Watch the listening positions of the user for changes, so other devices follow along while an episode is played somewhere else. | podcast | UserAuth | - | body:no
PUT /podcast/played/{episodeId} IPodcastService.setPlayed | Mark an episode as listened or as unlistened. Marking it as listened moves the position to the end of the episode, marking it as unlistened resets the position to the beginning. | podcast | UserAuth | episodeId:path,played:query | body:no
POST /podcast/refreshShow/{showId} IPodcastService.refreshShow | Fetch the feed of a show right now and store what changed. The call runs to completion before it returns and is skipped when the feed was already fetched less than 60 seconds ago. | podcast | UserAuth | showId:path | body:no
POST /podcast/reportPlayback IPodcastService.reportPlayback | Store the listening position of the user for an episode. A client reports on play, on pause, after a seek and every 10 to 15 seconds while playing, the same way song playback is reported. The last report wins, and the server marks an episode as completed on its own once the remaining time is under 30 seconds or under 5 percent of its length. | podcast | UserAuth | - | body:yes
POST /podcast/scanLocal IPodcastService.scanLocal | Scan the local podcast library for new, changed and vanished shows and episodes. The call runs to completion before it returns. | podcast | UserAuth | - | body:no
GET /podcast/show/{showId} IPodcastService.getShow | Read a single show. Returns null if the show does not exist. | podcast | UserAuth | showId:path | body:no
PUT /podcast/showSettings/{showId} IPodcastService.updateShowSettings | Change how the server keeps the episodes of a show. Switching a show to import makes the server store new episodes on disk, and the number of episodes to keep must be at least 1 when it is given. With newest retention the server imports the newest episodes and deletes everything beyond that count, while unlistened retention, which needs import delivery, imports the episodes nobody has finished yet and only deletes an episode once every subscriber listened to it to the end, with the keep count capping how many episodes are stored or queued at once. | podcast | UserAuth | showId:path | body:yes
GET /podcast/streamEpisode/{episodeId} IPodcastService.streamEpisode | Stream the audio of an episode. This is the only way a client plays an episode: the server serves the file when the episode is stored on it or belongs to the local podcast library, and relays the audio from its origin otherwise. Returns null if the episode has no audio at all. | podcast | UserAuth | episodeId:path,offset:query,chunkSize:query | body:no
HEAD /podcast/streamEpisode/{episodeId} IPodcastService.streamEpisode | Stream the audio of an episode. This is the only way a client plays an episode: the server serves the file when the episode is stored on it or belongs to the local podcast library, and relays the audio from its origin otherwise. Returns null if the episode has no audio at all. | podcast | UserAuth | episodeId:path,offset:query,chunkSize:query | body:no
GET /podcast/streamSize/{episodeId} IPodcastService.getStreamSize | Get the total size of the audio of an episode in bytes, or 0 if the size cannot be determined. | podcast | UserAuth | episodeId:path | body:no
POST /podcast/subscribe IPodcastService.subscribe | Subscribe to an RSS feed. The feed is fetched and parsed while the call runs when the server does not know it yet, so the call fails if the feed cannot be reached or is not a podcast feed. Subscribing again to a known feed is cheap and does not fetch anything. | podcast | UserAuth | feedUrl:query | body:no
POST /podcast/subscribeToShow/{showId} IPodcastService.subscribeToShow | Subscribe to a show the server already knows, for example one found through browseShows. | podcast | UserAuth | showId:path | body:no
GET /podcast/subscriptions IPodcastService.getSubscriptions | Read the shows the user is subscribed to, ordered by title. | podcast | UserAuth | - | body:no
GET /podcast/transcript/{transcriptId} IPodcastService.getTranscript | Read a single transcript together with its text. A transcript that only exists as a remote address is fetched once on first read and kept afterwards. Returns null if the transcript does not exist or its text cannot be obtained. | podcast | UserAuth | transcriptId:path | body:no
GET /podcast/transcripts/{episodeId} IPodcastService.getTranscripts | Read the transcripts known for an episode without their text. | podcast | UserAuth | episodeId:path | body:no
DELETE /podcast/unsubscribe/{showId} IPodcastService.unsubscribe | End the subscription of the user to a show. Returns false if the user was not subscribed. The show itself and its episodes stay on the server for a while after the last subscriber leaves. | podcast | UserAuth | showId:path | body:no
POST /queue/ackSynced IQueueService.ackSynced | Record that the calling session pulled the queue up to a version, so it can tell later whether the server state is newer than its own. | queue | UserAuth | version:query | body:no
POST /queue/beginUpload IQueueService.beginUpload | Start a chunked upload that replaces the whole queue. Entries are staged in memory with uploadPage and become visible only on commitUpload. Starting an upload discards any previous staged upload of the user, and a staged upload expires after a while if it is not committed. | queue | UserAuth | baseVersion:query,force:query | body:no
POST /queue/cancelUpload/{uploadId} IQueueService.cancelUpload | Discard a staged upload without touching the stored queue. | queue | UserAuth | uploadId:path | body:no
POST /queue/commitUpload/{uploadId} IQueueService.commitUpload | Replace the queue with the staged entries and store the supplied playback metadata. Entries referring to unknown songs are dropped and both orders are renumbered. When the upload answers a queue request of another device, its request identifier is passed so the requester is notified. | queue | UserAuth | uploadId:path,requestId:query | body:yes
PUT /queue/currentIndex IQueueService.setCurrentIndex | Set the entry that is currently playing, addressed by its index in the active order. The index is clamped to the size of the queue. | queue | UserAuth | baseVersion:query,currentIndex:query,force:query | body:no
DELETE /queue/entries IQueueService.remove | Remove entries from the queue by their queue identifiers. Unknown identifiers are ignored and the current index is adjusted to stay on the playing entry. | queue | UserAuth | baseVersion:query,queueIds:query,force:query | body:no
POST /queue/insert IQueueService.insert | Insert entries into the queue at a position of the active order (the shuffled order while shuffle is on, otherwise the original order). With shuffle on the entries are spliced into the shuffled order and appended to the end of the original order. | queue | UserAuth | baseVersion:query,position:query,force:query | body:yes
PUT /queue/modes IQueueService.setModes | Set shuffle and repeat mode. Enabling shuffle makes the server generate a shuffled order that starts with the entry that is currently playing, so the current index becomes 0; disabling it drops the shuffled order and puts the current index back on the original position of that entry. A player that shuffled on its own uploads its order instead. | queue | UserAuth | baseVersion:query,shuffleMode:query,repeatMode:query,force:query | body:no
POST /queue/move/{queueId} IQueueService.move | Move a single entry to another position of the active order (the shuffled order while shuffle is on, otherwise the original order). | queue | UserAuth | baseVersion:query,queueId:path,toPosition:query,force:query | body:no
GET /queue/observeQueue IQueueService.observeQueue | Watch the queue of the user for changes. A new metadata snapshot is emitted after every successful write, including writes made by other devices. | queue | UserAuth | - | body:no
GET /queue/queue IQueueService.getQueue | Read a page of queue entries, ordered by their position in the original order. Each entry also carries its shuffled position, and its song metadata only when the entries are requested with the songs resolved. | queue | UserAuth | page:query,pageSize:query,includeSongs:query | body:no
GET /queue/queueInfo IQueueService.getQueueInfo | Get the metadata of the queue without its entries. A user without a stored queue is reported at version 0 with no entries. | queue | UserAuth | - | body:no
POST /queue/requestUploadFrom/{sessionId} IQueueService.requestUploadFrom | Ask another device of the same user to upload its current queue and wait for the outcome. The request is delivered over the client request channel; sessions that are not listening are reported as unreachable and sessions that stay silent as timed out. | queue | UserAuth | sessionId:path | body:no
GET /queue/syncDevices IQueueService.getSyncDevices | List the devices of the user that take part in queue synchronization, including which entry is the calling session. | queue | UserAuth | - | body:no
PUT /queue/syncEnabled IQueueService.setSyncEnabled | Opt the calling session in or out of queue synchronization and record the name it is listed under on other devices. | queue | UserAuth | enabled:query,deviceName:query | body:no
POST /queue/uploadPage/{uploadId} IQueueService.uploadPage | Stage another page of entries for a started upload. Returns the total number of entries staged so far. | queue | UserAuth | uploadId:path | body:yes
